---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'hello@firstandlastpickleball.co.uk';
// Play night stats and player sign-in are described only once they are switched on.
const stats = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PLAY_CLOUD === 'on';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How firstandlastpickleball.co.uk handles your data — analytics, cookies, and the third parties we use.">
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">The boring but important bit</p>
      <h1>Privacy.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is a small website for a pickleball club. It collects almost nothing about you. Here's
        exactly what happens when you visit.
      </p>

      <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
      <p>
        firstandlastpickleball.co.uk is the website of First &amp; Last Pickleball Club, St Just. It's
        a simple informational site.{stats ? ' There are no accounts unless you are a club member who has asked to see their own play night stats (see below), and no forms that store your details.' : ' There are no accounts, no logins, and no forms that store your details.'} For any privacy question, email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What data the site holds about you</h2>
      <p>
        Browsing these pages doesn't require you to enter anything, and we don't ask you to. Two
        things are worth being explicit about:
      </p>

      <h3>1. Privacy-friendly analytics</h3>
      <p>
        We use <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vercel
        Web Analytics</a>, a privacy-focused tool that <strong>does not use cookies</strong>, does not
        track you across other websites, and does not collect any personally identifiable information.
        It records aggregate page views and referring domains so we know which parts of the site are
        useful — that's it. There's no advertising on this site and we don't sell or share any data.
      </p>

      <h3>2. When you click through to Spond or email us</h3>
      <p>
        Joining the club happens on <a href="https://spond.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spond</a>,
        a separate service with its own privacy policy — anything you enter there is governed by
        Spond, not this site. Likewise, if you email us, we'll hold your message (and your email
        address) only for as long as we need to reply and deal with it.
      </p>

      {stats && (
        <>
          <h2>Play night stats (club members)</h2>
          <p>
            If you play at our club nights, the people running the night keep a record so the night
            runs fairly, and so we can show you your own numbers.
          </p>
          <h3>What we hold</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>Your name, and your email if you gave it to a host so you can sign in.</li>
            <li>Which nights you came to, cancelled, or did not turn up to.</li>
            <li>Who you played with and against, and the scores of your games.</li>
            <li>For under 18s: that they are under 18, and whether a parent or guardian has agreed to them being shown on the leaderboard.</li>
            <li>Hosts may also note a player's level (for example Beginner or Improver) to organise fair matches. Players do not see these notes.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Why, and your choices</h3>
          <p>
            We keep this record to run play nights (who is coming, who plays whom), to show members
            their own stats, and to run a club leaderboard. We rely on our legitimate interest in
            running the club for the record keeping. The leaderboard is opt-out: you can switch
            yourself off at any time on the <a href="/me">Your stats</a> page. Under 18s are not
            shown on the leaderboard unless a parent or guardian has said yes.
          </p>
          <h3>Who can see it</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li><strong>Hosts</strong> (committee members and volunteers who run the nights) can see everything above.</li>
            <li><strong>You</strong> can see your own numbers and your own attendance.</li>
            <li><strong>Other members</strong> see only your name, games played, win percentage and points difference on the leaderboard, and only if you have not switched it off. Attendance and no-shows are never shown to other players.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Where it is kept, and for how long</h3>
          <p>
            The record is held in a Supabase database in London, and sign-in links are sent by email.
            We keep your record while you play with us, and delete it if you ask. Deleting your record
            removes your attendance and any level notes. The scores of games you played stay in the
            record for other players, without your name.
          </p>
          <p>
            To see everything we hold about you, correct it, or have it deleted, email
            <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      <h2>Cookies in use</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>None.</strong> This site sets no cookies — not for analytics, not for anything. There's
        no cookie banner because there's nothing to consent to.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>The site relies on these providers to function:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>
          <strong>Vercel</strong> — hosting and analytics. To serve a page, Vercel processes the
          minimum necessary request data (your IP address, browser type and the URL requested).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Spond</strong> — only if you follow a link to join the club. Spond has its own
          privacy policy that applies once you're on their site or app.
        </li>
        {stats && (
          <li>
            <strong>Supabase</strong> — stores the play night record described above, and handles
            sign-in. Used only by club members and the hosts who run play nights.
          </li>
        )}
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights under UK GDPR</h2>
      <p>{stats ? 'These are simple to exercise:' : 'Because the site stores virtually nothing about you, these are simple to exercise:'}</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li><strong>Access &amp; erasure:</strong> {stats ? 'for the play night record, email us and we will send you what we hold or delete it. Aggregate analytics data is not personally identifiable. For anything held in our email, contact us below.' : "there's no account or server-side profile to access or delete. Aggregate analytics data is not personally identifiable. For anything held in our email, contact us below."}</li>
        <li><strong>Complain:</strong> you can complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>) at any time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about any of this? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we'll do our best to help.
      </p>

      <p class="footer-note">Last updated: {stats ? 'November 2026' : 'June 2026'}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 46rem; }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  h2:first-of-type { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; }
  h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .bullets {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .bullets li {
    padding: 0.55rem 0 0.55rem 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--line);
  }
  .bullets li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .bullets li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 1.05rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--coral);
  }
  .footer-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--sea-light);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
